<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>At least two killed in fire caused by 'massive strikes' on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0237f8b4a3f29001c1c97fa2412b027d1f2c7df7b543c40b318a657af93f9a4a</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:56:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-at-least-two-killed-in-fire-caused-by-massive-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">At least two people were killed in a fire in Kyiv after what President Volodymyr Zelensky described as"massive strikes" on the Ukrainian capital on Wednesday. Ukraine has come under increased attack in recent weeks as Russian attacks have targeted energy infrastructure and rail and road transport.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Lionel Messi scores as Argentina beat Benin for his last international game</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:701ca324c875c9e9526f4cc16868467eb671c6adadd35fc28205777f7965fb7b</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:42:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261007-lionel-messi-scores-as-argentina-beat-benin-for-his-last-international-game" /><summary type="html">Lionel Messi played his final match for Argentina, a 3-0 victory over Benin. A full tribute was paid to him before and after the match.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How Netanyahu survived the political fallout from the October 7 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db48e98415954bda99b9a17e572bde3987369abaf8c9e4653461ac99bd3a880a</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:24:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-how-netanyahu-survived-the-political-fallout-from-the-october-7-attacks" /><summary type="html">Three years after the deadly Hamas-led October 7 attacks in southern Israel, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is fighting for political survival ahead of legislative elections later this month. Reports that Arab leaders warned him of the assault in advance have undercut his claims that Israel's security chiefs are to blame, but his political base appears to be holding.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Houthis target airport in Yemen as Israel marks October 7 anniversary</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a63184dfaf8a52f329e89cb1e9081427c52e29432bcf679b9c9f57ef68a58096</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:46:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-middle-east-live-houthis-target-airport-in-yemen-as-israel-marks-october-7-anniversary" /><summary type="html">Two missiles launched by Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels targeted Aden's international airport early Wednesday, with no casualties reported, as Israel prepared to mark the third anniversary of the October 7, 2023 Hamas attacks. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel marks third anniversary of October 7 attack as election looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:656af0c07bbf07c7188e1e38123264a656cb33be8756a786230f76732d4b155b</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:14:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-marks-third-anniversary-of-october-7-attack-as-election-looms" /><summary type="html">Israel will mark the third anniversary of the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack on Wednesday with memorial events across the country, as heightened security surrounds the commemorations and voters prepare for an election in which the deadliest day in Israel’s history is expected to remain a central issue.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Messi bids farewell to Argentina fans in emotional international finale</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8896493de7e11aa48aa086e1f981bf44ef95059ab8f236231e13eff143ec4fb4</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T01:59:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261007-messi-bids-farewell-to-argentina-fans-in-emotional-international-finale" /><summary type="html">Lionel Messi said farewell to Argentina fans Tuesday in an emotional final international appearance, scoring in a 3-0 win over Benin at Buenos Aires' Monumental Stadium as 85,000 supporters celebrated the end of a career that brought the country its long-awaited 2022 World Cup triumph.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Haiti postpones elections indefinitely as gang violence hampers preparations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dd87a0d42437e90e834fecd8da3fb2aeda1e1d5bdbb7479b68b4746b42dccb2</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T01:06:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-haiti-postpones-elections-indefinitely-as-gang-violence-hampers-preparations" /><summary type="html">Haiti has indefinitely postponed elections scheduled for December and February, the electoral council said Tuesday, citing technical and operational requirements as gang violence continues to disrupt preparations. The delay leaves Haitians without a vote as authorities struggle to register voters and secure areas needed for the poll.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Christa Pike regains consciousness after botched Tennessee execution attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9347e8a07b9b2f681a18cec3d7b5d3c1a641aa95aa318509b6431d24c873e06b</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T23:30:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-christa-pike-regains-consciousness-after-botched-tennessee-execution-attempt" /><summary type="html">Convicted murderer Christa Pike regained consciousness and began speaking Tuesday after surviving a botched execution by lethal injection. Pike, the first woman the state of Tennessee has attempted to put to death in 200 years, remains hospitalised with severe injuries to both arms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says he will speak to Putin over reported plague death in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db6522c3882df512383c457f91f3c319e54ffc8a2bef9083a5afbe71a9788a9f</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T22:51:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-trump-says-he-will-speak-to-putin-over-reported-plague-death-in-russia" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Tuesday he would speak “very soon” with Russian President Vladimir Putin over the reported plague death of a laboratory technician, as Washington and the World Health Organization pressed Moscow for greater transparency and clarity over conflicting accounts of the incident in Siberia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's former spy chief detained on suspicion of trading state secrets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2551bf144a26e73b41dc4c748171b87f73f3520cc5f0b92d5cb85e29b871303d</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T21:34:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-former-german-spy-chief-detained-over-suspected-treasonous-espionage" /><summary type="html">Former German spy chief August Hanning was detained Tuesday on suspicion of treason and espionage after prosecutors accused him of paying for secret intelligence documents and using them to prepare an analysis for a foreign intelligence service, in a case that could strain Berlin’s ties with allied spy agencies.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports first-ever Ebola death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f49ded719a13f1b791e37949f58443bedc687cc11cf4cad67447293588ea6ba</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T21:28:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Kenya records its first Ebola death after a man travelled from the DRC via Uganda. Also, Comoros is tightening the rules on who can do business. In South Africa, concerns are growing that xenophobia and hostility toward foreign nationals could be driving African tourists away.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Cancer rates rising faster among younger people, international study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99f6d5f0bd34a249c682fdee1ba34cb88336d3e433c730ef168c838a5b03b878</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T21:10:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-cancer-rates-rising-faster-among-younger-people-international-study-finds" /><summary type="html">New major research has found that cases of several different kinds of cancer have risen sharply among young people in England, the US, and in the Netherlands. The number of people under the age of 50 diagnosed with prostate cancer in England has quadrupled since 2001. Researchers aren't exactly sure why there's been such an increase but say the broad reason could be linked to a growing rate of obesity, poor diets and a lack of exercise. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Jon Shelton, Head of cancer intelligence at Cancer Research UK.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Cancer rates rising faster among younger people, international study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbaf9d578b33c896b3abc409375c846be4ab59f65c412242879c3cb860fe8581</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T21:09:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cancer-rates-rising-faster-among-younger-people-international-study-finds" /><summary type="html">New major research has found that cases of several different kinds of cancer have risen sharply among young people in England, the US, and in the Netherlands. The number of people under the age of 50 diagnosed with prostate cancer in England has quadrupled since 2001. Researchers aren't exactly sure why there's been such an increase but say the broad reason could be linked to a growing rate of obesity, poor diets and a lack of exercise. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Jon Shelton, Head of cancer intelligence at Cancer Research UK.</summary></entry><entry><title>French policeman charged after firing tear gas grenade at high school student</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb58c9a1f005ae016c07215828f2389b1dd0b710e19b1f9da5e839053b9b8b9e</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T21:04:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-policeman-charged-after-firing-tear-gas-grenade-at-high-school-student" /><summary type="html">A French policeman was charged Tuesday with violence for firing a tear gas grenade at close range at a 14-year-old student during high school protests that have shaken the country. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Fanny Gallois, Head of the Freedoms Program, Amnesty International, says that "these cases of serious injuries related to the use of so-called less-lethal weapons commonly used in France are specifically worrying because we've been asking for their ban for years" adding that "the kind of weapons that are being used and the kind of injuries caused are extremely worrying for a country such as France".</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian lab worker’s death sparks plague fears as unverified claims spread online</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30528a539a3ba2bd04021749e8645498763502cb7b14456b3b24509cd23fa82a</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-lab-worker-s-death-sparks-plague-fears-as-unverified-claims-spread-online-1" /><summary type="html">The death of a 28-year-old Russian lab worker at Siberia’s Irkutsk Anti-Plague Institute has sparked online panic about a ‘plague’, despite the WHO assessing the public health risk in Russia as low. Unverified claims about how she became ill, including a laboratory accident involving a test tube, are circulating online. Misleading posts and out-of-context videos have also fuelled speculation and fear. Vedika Bahl goes through them, and what we know, in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>How much does France spend on education?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8be8aaa7b2b4abbfd86d0fb1c7dcd3845e38da10f460bb2d4f34cb5cca7e005</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T20:29:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261006-how-much-does-france-spend-on-education" /><summary type="html">Protests have been gripping France with students demanding better learning conditions and more equal opportunities. The education ministry is among the few that have been granted an increase in next year's draft budgets, but critics say it still doesn't catch up with inflation.  We take a closer look.  Plus, OpenAI has apologised to Australia over its handling of government website hacks by a rogue AI agent in June.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Police make seventh arrest over UK airbase incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60bdd7d611497712b5a923a930d8e8301399f95d0d41ebd4be5e03a3ab2b6f8c</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:51:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident--a2cfc3b816d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident" /><summary type="html">A seventh man was arrested Tuesday over a major incident last month at a British military airbase used by the United States to launch strikes on Iran, police said. The arrest came a day after President Donald Trump said the United States had withdrawn all B-1 bombers from RAF Fairford because of "threats" he believed were linked to Tehran. A 22-year-old British male was arrested in London "on suspicion of preparation of terrorist acts", Britain's Counter-Terrorism Policing network said in a statement. Six men in their 20s have already been arrested and released on bail after three suspicious vans were stopped near the base in southwest England on September 27. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London.</summary></entry><entry><title>Calls to block social media platforms for minors in France amid school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b7c79d6ef95574dcfb4fd9f4d42a488609766d6aa3bafeaa9353a06de07ff84</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:47:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/calls-to-block-social-media-platforms-for-minors-in-france-amid-school-protests--b44929c55975.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/calls-to-block-social-media-platforms-for-minors-in-france-amid-school-protests" /><summary type="html">One factor accelerating these student protest is social media, and its being boosted even more by artificial intelligence. Some French mayors have even called for social media platforms to be temporarily blocked for minors. Our colleauges at France 2 took a look at the impact</summary></entry><entry><title>German ex-spy chief arrested for suspected espionage, treason</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5babfdabdd4950f976dc6d0ee1643083a96a23972837b014ed0796f994656d2</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:42:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason--cbca89fe2a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason" /><summary type="html">A former German spy chief was arrested Tuesday on suspicion of espionage and treason, an embarrassing case at a time when the country is seeking to broaden the powers of its intelligence agencies. August Hanning, who ran Germany's BND foreign intelligence agency from 1998 to 2005, is accused of espionage, treason and working for foreign intelligence services, federal prosecutors said. FRANCE 24's Nick Holdsworth reports from Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>'We're fed up': Paris students rise up in a movement that shows no sign of slowing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b61093ba94a92a83c70f971bd55fcd94527864da3f9c765ae0828d7d612a187</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:41:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261006-we-re-fed-up-paris-students-rise-up-in-a-movement-that-shows-no-sign-of-slowing--af976d777fba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261006-we-re-fed-up-paris-students-rise-up-in-a-movement-that-shows-no-sign-of-slowing" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of students and their supporters took part in nationwide protests across France on Tuesday after weeks of student barricades protesting school conditions.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Students, unions and teachers in mass movement to demand better learning conditions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53dd6ece4cde1761fc2313d1cc7f265748156321c7d4b1cbb705dfbdef10c93e</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:39:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/students-unions-and-teachers-in-mass-movement-to-demand-better-learning-conditions--8c9b78ca5575.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/students-unions-and-teachers-in-mass-movement-to-demand-better-learning-conditions" /><summary type="html">A quarter of a million demonstrators took to the streets across France on Tuesday as unions and teachers joined high school students demanding better learning conditions in protests that later descended into sporadic clashes with security forces. A French policeman was on Tuesday charged with violence over the firing of a tear gas grenade last week at close range at a 14-year-old student during the high school protests that have shaken the country, the prosecutor said. Reporting from central Paris, FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin says the protesters are adamant that "this is not it, this movement will continue, we want concrete actions from the government".</summary></entry><entry><title>France erupts overs schools: Why the violence surrounding surprise movement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acadfed9e9e64bed113aa712ab986b022fbfaa8ed92b1d8426e3762626b68199</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261006-france-erupts-overs-schools-why-the-violence-surrounding-surprise-movement--c22593653ff3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261006-france-erupts-overs-schools-why-the-violence-surrounding-surprise-movement" /><summary type="html">It’s a protest movement that a broke, lame-duck French government did not see coming. Civil servants this Tuesday joining high schoolers now in their third week of picketing over long-deteriorating classroom conditions. The usual recipe for wearing down movements in France has recently been to match eventual violence with a heavy hand, the escalation turning the silent majority against the protesters as was the case with the pre-Covid Yellow Vests movement.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'Colossal failure: Death penalty system in America is a broken process from start to finish'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1e3f5e6ee7cd194b4f169d04bc85bb4f29d3779687c7fa0997ea81c1aa327a7</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish--4aeddd5f6ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Reed Brody, international human rights lawyer and former New York assistant attorney general. According to Brody, the botched execution of Christa Pike reflects a much larger problem: the relationship between capital punishment, institutional failure, due process, and human dignity. The technical failure of lethal injection exposes weaknesses throughout the legal architecture surrounding the death penalty, from the quality and adequacy of defense representation to the profound disparities between jurisdictions and the difficulties states face in administering executions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cecb29b93c7d6a9c8e813213a9825eeac58c280b395ed114711f1d7d750b694b</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:05:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says--0d01da482669.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry></feed>
